  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "overview",
      "title": "Model overview and intended purpose",
      "status": "available",
      "source": "llm_draft",
      "text": "Legacy R Logistic Regression (legacy-r-logistic) estimates the probability that a credit-card customer defaults next month and is described as being used in credit decisions; this purpose was inferred rather than confirmed, and the business owner, intended use and decision context are not documented. The model is assigned risk tier 1. It was developed on the public UCI Default of Credit Card Clients dataset (30,000 records, Taiwan, April to September 2005). That data is for demonstration only and is not representative of a UK bank's current portfolio.",
      "rows": []
    },
    {
