    {
      "key": "methodology",
      "title": "Algorithm and methodology",
      "status": "available",
      "source": "llm_draft",
      "text": "The model is a logistic regression fitted in R with glm (binomial family, logit link). It uses 21 inputs: LIMIT_BAL, EDUCATION, MARRIAGE, PAY_0 and PAY_2 to PAY_6, BILL_AMT1 to BILL_AMT6, and PAY_AMT1 to PAY_AMT6. SEX, AGE, ID and row_id are excluded from the predictors, and the target is default.payment.next.month. Upstream Python code makes a stratified 80/20 train/test split (random_state=42), and a hard-coded threshold of 0.35 converts probabilities to classes. The reported test results are accuracy 0.807, ROC AUC 0.707, precision 0.592 and recall 0.412, and the R predictions match a statsmodels reimplementation within a 1e-05 tolerance (100% classification agreement).",
      "rows": []
    },
